1. **`SwingUtilities.invokeLater()`** - Ensures the GUI is created on the Event Dispatch Thread (EDT), which is the recommended practice for Swing applications.

2. **`JFrame`** - Creates the main window with the title "Simple Window".

3. **`setSize(400, 300)`** - Sets the window dimensions to 400 pixels wide and 300 pixels tall.

4. **`setLocationRelativeTo(null)`** - Centers the window on the screen.

5. **`setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE)`** - Ensures the application terminates when the window is closed.

6. **`setVisible(true)`** - Makes the window visible on screen.

